402:## 14. Superoptimization
404:A **superoptimizer** searches for the shortest (or cheapest) instruction sequence equivalent to a given one, instead of improving the given one by rules. Massalin coined the term and searched exhaustively over short sequences (*Superoptimizer: A Look at the Smallest Program*, ASPLOS 1987). Later systems made the search practical:
406:- **Learned peephole rules.** Bansal and Aiken harvested short windows from real programs, superoptimized them offline, and stored the results as a table of peephole rules (*Automatic Generation of Peephole Superoptimizers*, ASPLOS 2006).
407:- **Stochastic search.** STOKE, by Schkufza, Sharma and Aiken, searches by Markov-chain sampling (*Stochastic Superoptimization*, ASPLOS 2013).
