123:There is a precedent for a contract that deliberately accepts a program that does not mean the same thing as r0 everywhere. `Program.assume(bindings)` restricts the meaning check to inputs satisfying an assumption, and specialization on outer facts uses it. The assumption is stored with each revision made under it (IRWB-002 guide section 10, "Assumptions"). A tolerance revision needs the same kind of bookkeeping: a revision that is not exact, together with the reason it was accepted.
