245:4. **Linear metrics are decided by fireflies.** In S-02, one sample in pass 30 has luminance 7.39 × 10⁵, while the frame mean in the other passes inspected is 5.8 to 11.2. That one sample makes the linear RMS difference of the two 16-pass means larger than that of two single passes (relative RMS 2.4 against 0.021). In B-01 and S-02, the largest 1 % of squared differences carry 87 % of the total at n = 1. **A tolerance must be stated on the displayed image (or a robust statistic), not on raw radiance.** S-02 also shows that spectral rendering produces negative colour channels: about 380 of its 400 pixels have a negative r, g or b in every pass, which the display map clamps to 0.
